The 0.94 upstream release of qpsmtpd renamed the various 'check_' plugins
to use names without the check_ prefix, amongst other updates.  While
upstream believes the new versions to be interface-compatible with their
predecessors, the actual names are changed.  Note that check_spamhelo was
not simply renamed: its replacement is called 'helo'.

The check_* plugins shipped with this package are thin transitional
wrappers which expose the new plugins under their old names.  They log a
deprecation warning on every start and may be dropped in a future release,
so please migrate your configuration.  The following shell snippet does
that for you:

    cp /etc/qpsmtpd/plugins /etc/qpsmtpd/plugins.orig
    for p in earlytalker relay badmailfrom badrcptto loop ; do
      perl -pi -e 's/^(# |)check_('$p')\b/$1$2/' /etc/qpsmtpd/plugins
    done
    perl -pi -e 's/^(# |)check_spamhelo\b/${1}helo/' /etc/qpsmtpd/plugins

Two further plugins referenced by older Debian configurations were renamed
as well:

    require_resolvable_fromhost  ->  resolvable_fromhost
    badrcptto_patterns           ->  rcpt_regexp   (different config format,
                                                    see its POD)
